# 6. Time and Space Complexity

This is extremely important for your practical viva.

### Time Complexity

According to your manual:

\[
\boxed{O(n\log n)}
\]

Where n is the number of unique characters.

**Why?**

- Building the Min Heap takes O(n).
- Extracting the two minimum nodes takes O(log n) per extraction.
- We perform n−1 merging operations.
- Each merge requires heap operations.

Therefore:

\[
O(n\log n)
\]

### Space Complexity

The auxiliary space complexity is:

\[
\boxed{O(n)}
\]

Because we store:
- The frequency of each character.
- The Min Heap.
- The Huffman Tree.
- The generated codes.

Here, n represents the number of unique characters.

The manual also mentions that if the input array is sorted, a linear-time algorithm exists. Assignment No 2 DAA

